  "notes": [
    "Native Android arm64 CLI: separate historical component tests and one completed 28-step, 56-forward phone generation. No APK/camera integration.",
    "VAE is one 512x512 person tile; garment uses posterior-mean export fixture; tryon uses a synthetic seeded sample, reference garment features and cached image embeddings.",
    "Corrected runner refreshes each input by reading one file at a time before every measured forward.",
    "Tryon streamed-input runner completed 3 phone forwards at about 24.06 s each; output relative RMSE is 0.2965 versus the FP32 PyTorch fixture.",
    "Nonquantized garment CPU control matches the reference; INT4 CPU and OpenCL controls show similar residual error, attributing the garment error to this MNN INT4 candidate rather than OpenCL alone.",
    "Latency includes forward and output download, excludes loading, session/kernel creation, input refresh, warmup and file saving.",
    "Peak RSS can include GPU mappings but not all driver allocations. Do not add component peaks or treat them as full-pipeline memory.",
    "Backend 3 output placement does not prove every kernel exclusively executes on the GPU.",
    "Full scheduler, sequential CFG, six-tile person VAE and final decoder completed on phone in 2081 s; initial CFG/Euler and VAE blending math checks are exact.",
    "Tryon INT8 MNN model is 391MiB; host CPU control completed in 16.40 s with relative RMSE 0.02690 and peak RSS 2.13GiB.",
    "Tryon FP16 MNN model is 731MiB; Pixel 4 run was terminated at RSS 2.246GiB with 30,436KiB MemAvailable before producing output.",
    "Tryon INT8 OpenCL completed one Pixel 4 forward in 25.46 s with 1.815GiB peak RSS; MemAvailable reached 180,016KiB and output was finite.",
    "The preliminary top8 exclusion heuristic used a channel-product proxy that omitted convolution groups; its Pixel 4 relative RMSE 0.53436 is not calibrated sensitivity evidence.",
    "Structural INT4/FP16 with block32 completed three Pixel 4 OpenCL Low forwards at 24.511 s average, 1.589 GiB peak RSS and relative RMSE 0.08390; block size and preserved layers changed together.",
    "Zero-input auto-quant fixtures were used only to enumerate layer metadata, not for calibration or accuracy. Their rate=0 is not an evaluation result.",
    "OpenCL Low precision=2 uses half storage/compute; Normal precision=0 uses half storage/float compute. Weight storage and runtime arithmetic precision are separate.",
    "The same structural mixed model with OpenCL Normal precision=0 measured 31.178 s over three forwards, 1.602 GiB peak RSS and relative RMSE 0.08466. Low is the follow-up candidate on this fixture; these sequential timing measurements do not isolate thermal/DVFS effects.",
    "Numerical comparisons use the final saved forward only; three timing repeats do not establish agreement across inputs or timesteps.",
    "Full-generation cache is 1,849,688,064 bytes per fixed garment/latent/seed/scheduler; this experiment does not establish a practical catalog storage solution.",
    "Full generation includes model/session setup, neural execution, cache IO, CPU scheduler/CFG/blending and checkpoint writes; excludes offline precompute, ADB transfer, JPEG preparation and host PNG encoding.",
    "Denoising forward/download alone took 1647.47 seconds; this Pixel 4 OpenCL implementation is rejected for practical latency."
  ],
